# C# quality

- Use file-scoped namespaces and nullable reference types.
- Prefer explicit public APIs on `GameSimulation` over mutating internals from adapters.
- Keep gameplay rules out of SFML/Client projects.
- Do not suppress analyzer warnings without a short comment explaining why.
- After edits run `dotnet build SteelConveyorWar.sln -c Release` and relevant tests.
- Prefer renaming placeholder files over leaving `Class1.cs` / `UnitTest1.cs`.

```csharp
// ❌ BAD — gameplay mutation in adapter / bypassing commands
entity.Health -= 10;

// ✅ GOOD — production mutation via public command API
simulation.TryQueueCommanderMove(playerId, commanderId, target);

// ✅ GOOD — test-only damage remains internal (Core.Tests via InternalsVisibleTo)
simulation.DamageEntity(entity.Id, 10);
```
